# SEO strategy

Do not build the entire SEO strategy around “Pay Per Call.” It is a specialization; visibility spans four layers:

1. **Outcome:** Customer Acquisition, Lead Generation, Inbound Customer Acquisition, Customer Acquisition Services  
2. **Category:** Performance Marketing, Performance Marketing Agency, Performance Advertising  
3. **Engine:** Media Buying, Performance Media Buying, Paid Media, Digital Customer Acquisition  
4. **Specialization:** Pay Per Call, Pay Per Call Marketing/Agency/Network, Inbound Call Generation, Call Generation Services  

These are seed concepts — research SERPs before locking targets. Prefer commercial intent and conversion potential over raw volume.

## Page ownership (no cannibalization)

| Page | Owns |
| --- | --- |
| Home | Broader performance customer acquisition / brand |
| Performance Marketing | Performance Marketing Services |
| Media Buying | Performance Media Buying |
| Pay Per Call | Pay Per Call Marketing |
| Inbound Call Generation | Inbound Call Generation Services |
| Advertisers/Buyers | Performance customer acquisition for advertisers |
| Publishers | Pay Per Call publisher network / media partnerships |
| Industry pages | Industry-specific acquisition intent only |

One primary keyword concept per major page unless there is a strategic reason to share.

## Target architecture (evolve with research)

HOME · ABOUT · SOLUTIONS (Performance Marketing, Media Buying, Pay Per Call, Inbound Call Generation) · FOR ADVERTISERS · FOR PUBLISHERS · INDUSTRIES (approved verticals only) · RESOURCES (clusters below) · CONTACT

## Content clusters (prioritize by commercial relevance + research)

- Customer Acquisition · Performance Marketing · Media Buying · Pay Per Call · Inbound Call Generation  
- Industry SEO (Insurance, Home Services, Legal, Financial) only for supported verticals; pages must be truly industry-specific

## Blog & resources

Prioritize topics by commercial relevance — do not auto-write every cluster idea. Length follows search intent (no padding). Competitor sites = intelligence for intent/gaps only — never copy sentences, headings, slogans, structure, or claims.

## On-page keyword use

Primary phrase once in H1 or opening; secondary/semantic terms in H2s naturally. Meta title/description align with page-owned concept and hero promise.
